      "sortOrder": 40,
      "notes": "Q3 2026 13F (filed 2026-11-16 by parent Pershing Square Inc.): $30.80B across 16 positions. Largest: Pershing Square Inc. (PS) $10.31B, Uber $2.35B, Amazon $2.12B, Microsoft $2.08B, Meta $2.05B. New in Q3: Intercontinental Exchange $1.01B and Alcon $954M (CINS H01301128, unlinked until the 2026-11-17 resolver fix); Hertz exited. The 184.3M-share PS stake first appeared in a 13F-HR/A NEW HOLDINGS amendment for Q2 filed the same day, which lifted Q2 from $19.47B to $25.52B. Famous big bets include the Herbalife short, the FNMA/FMCC preferreds, and a major stake in Fannie Mae bonds. Public letters often precede activist campaigns.",
      "photoUrl": "/avatars/ackman.jpg",
      "photoCredit": "Senate Democrats · CC BY 2.0 (Wikimedia)",
      "infoText": "Founder and CEO of Pershing Square Capital Management (founded 2004). Runs one of the most concentrated activist books on Wall Street, typically 10–15 positions. Known for the Herbalife short (eventually closed at a loss), the FNMA/FMCC preferreds bet, and ahead-of-the-news public letters. Since Q2 2026 the 13F is filed by the public parent, Pershing Square Inc. (NYSE: PS). Its largest line as of September 30 2026 is a 184.3M-share stake in Pershing Square Inc. itself, $10.3B of a $30.8B book.",
